      "description": "Not windowed: a dead letter from last night is still a dead letter this morning, and an alert that only looked at the last hour would go quiet overnight and leave the queue to be discovered by whoever noticed the missing work. Warning rather than critical because the retries have already happened \u2014 nothing is getting worse while somebody reads this \u2014 but it does not clear on its own, which is the point.",
      "runbook": "Open the queue health page, filter the job list to DISCARDED, and read the attempts on one: every failure is kept with what it said and how long it ran. Fix the cause, then retry \u2014 a retry resets the attempt count, so the policy applies again from the start."
