    },
    "annotations": {
      "summary": "More than a quarter of attempts on some job type are failing.",
      "description": "Attempts rather than jobs: a job that retries three times and then succeeds is counted as two failures here, which is deliberate \u2014 it is the signal that arrives before the dead letters do. clamp_min keeps a single failure on an idle night from reading as 100%.",
      "runbook": "Read one failing job's attempts on the queue health page. A failure that is the same error every time is a bug or a dependency that is down; failures that differ are usually load. If the kind is doing damage while it fails, pause it \u2014 that is what the pause button is for, and it takes effect on the next poll without a deploy."
    }
